+
+When a device-memory allocation fails, the allocator releases completely empty pooled spares
+of every memory type, then retries only if memory was actually returned. It performs at most
+one such reclamation pass per placement; the existing smaller-growth-block fallback remains.
+Live placements, pending work and caller imports are never reclaimed, and block indices remain
+stable. WorkCounts exposes reclaimed empty blocks and bytes; system process limits are unchanged.
